1.1 Introduction to reactive
============================

The ‘reactive’ package gives Maxima first-class *signals*.  A signal is
a named, bounded, mutable numeric value that appears in expressions as a
noun form printed ‘signal(name)’.  Maxima keeps the noun form symbolic
through simplification, ‘diff’, ‘integrate’, ‘limit’, ‘solve’ and
‘subst’, so an expression built from signals keeps its dependency on
them.  The noun's argument is a symbol from a private Lisp package, so a
user variable with the same name as a signal never captures it.

Downstream packages such as ‘ax-plots’ walk an expression with
‘collect_signals’, emit a UI control for each signal, and call
‘resolve_signals’ to substitute current values before sampling.  When a
control moves, the host calls ‘signal_set’ and re-evaluates the view.

To use the package:

load("reactive");

