1.1.2 Names
-----------

A signal name is a string of 1 to 128 ASCII letters, digits or
underscores.  The constructors reject anything else, because the aximar
host applies the same rule when a slider moves.  Names are
case-sensitive: ‘"freq"’ and ‘"Freq"’ are different signals.


File: reactive.info,  Node: Registry,  Next: Limitations,  Prev: Names,  Up: Introduction to reactive

1.1.3 Registry
--------------

Each signal lives in a per-session registry keyed by name.  An entry is
a list of ‘key = value’ equations:

[name = "freq", kind = slider, lo = 0.1, hi = 5.0, value = 0.1]

   • ‘lo’, ‘hi’ and ‘value’ are floats.
   • ‘kind’ is one of ‘slider’, ‘number’, ‘checkbox’, ‘dropdown’.
   • Dropdowns add ‘choices = [...]’.

Read fields with ‘signal_field’, ‘signal_value’ or ‘signal_kind’ rather
than by position.  New widget kinds will add fields.

Calling a ‘widget_*’ constructor with an existing name replaces that
entry.  Re-running a notebook cell therefore resets the signal to its
initial value.


File: reactive.info,  Node: Limitations,  Prev: Registry,  Up: Introduction to reactive

1.1.4 Limitations
-----------------

   • Numeric evaluation does not resolve signals automatically.  Call
     ‘resolve_signals’ before ‘float’, plotting or sampling.
     (‘ax-plots’ does this for you.)
   • ‘signal_set’ does not clamp slider or number values to ‘[lo, hi]’.
     The caller (normally the renderer) enforces the range.
   • The package has no event-bound widgets yet (buttons, click or drag
     on a plot).


