 -- Function: signal_set (TARGET, VALUE)
     Sets the current value of a signal and returns the new value as a
     float.  ‘target’ may be a signal noun form or a name string.

        • For a checkbox, ‘value’ may be ‘true’, ‘false’, ‘0’ or ‘1’.
          Anything else is an error.
        • For a dropdown, ‘value’ must be one of the registered choices.
        • For a slider or number, any number is accepted and not
          clamped.

     (%i1) widget_slider("freq", 0.1, 5)$
     (%i2) signal_set("freq", 2.5);
     (%o2)                           2.5


File: reactive.info,  Node: Function collect_signals expr,  Next: Function resolve_signals expr,  Prev: Function signal_set target value,  Up: Definitions for reactive

 -- Function: collect_signals (EXPR)
     Returns the names of the signals that appear in ‘expr’, each once,
     in the order a depth-first walk of the simplified expression first
     meets them.  Maxima may reorder terms during simplification, so the
     order can differ from the order in your input.

     (%i1) a : widget_slider("a", 0, 1)$
     (%i2) b : widget_slider("b", 0, 1)$
     (%i3) collect_signals(a*x + b*sin(a*x));
     (%o3)                         [b, a]


File: reactive.info,  Node: Function resolve_signals expr,  Next: Function reactive_reset,  Prev: Function collect_signals expr,  Up: Definitions for reactive

 -- Function: resolve_signals (EXPR)
     Returns ‘expr’ with every signal replaced by its current value.
     Returns ‘expr’ unchanged if it has no signals.  Signals an error if
     ‘expr’ names a signal that is no longer registered.


File: reactive.info,  Node: Function reactive_reset,  Prev: Function resolve_signals expr,  Up: Definitions for reactive

 -- Function: reactive_reset ()
     Clears the registry.  Noun forms created before the reset still
     exist, but ‘signal_value’ and ‘resolve_signals’ fail on them until
     you register the names again.  Tests and notebook restarts use
     this.


